  "verbalization": "Viscidulin Iii appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. The evidence suggests that Viscidulin Iii interacts with the Interferon alpha/beta receptor (IFNAR), which is a known target of several compounds, including those that are involved in immune responses. This pathway is further linked to the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein, indicating a potential role in immune modulation. Additionally, Viscidulin Iii is also shown to target Taste receptor type 2 member 31, which, although less well-characterized, may contribute to similar biological processes. The integration of these targets highlights a possible mechanism by which Viscidulin Iii influences macrophage function, potentially through the activation of signaling pathways that regulate gene expression. The evidence supports a broad, interconnected network of interactions, where Viscidulin Iii acts as a modulator of immune-related pathways, ultimately affecting the expression of the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein.",
